  "summary": "The schematic is consistent with the intended Hades design: power rails, current-sense path (R1=10mΩ into INA219 @0x40), buck feedback (R5=6k8/R6=1k3 giving Vout=0.8*(1+R5/R6)≈5V), 3.3V LDO, both MCUs, crystals, I2C/SPI/GPIO/UART cross-links and sensor set all match the spec. The barometer RESET/EOC and pull-up mix-up is a documented known bug (not an anomaly), and the PCA9685 note reading 0x41 on the same I2C2 bus as the INA219 (0x40) is the correct strapping that avoids an address conflict, so the spec table's '0x40' for the PWM driver is a spec-side transcription slip rather than a deviation in the board files; no board-level anomaly is supported by the drawing."
}

